It contains a Rust port of parts of brlaser, the CUPS driver for Brother
laser printers by Peter De Wachter (https://github.com/pdewacht/brlaser,
version 6, commit 2a49e3287c70c254e7e3ac9dabe9d6a07218c3fa), licensed
GPL-2.0-or-later. Copyright 2013 Peter De Wachter.

What was ported, and from where:

  src/encode.rs
    - brlaser src/line.cc: encode_line (with and without a reference line),
      write_overflow, write_substitute, write_repeat, substitute_length,
      repeat_length, the 254-edit cap and the 0xFF blank-line code.
    - brlaser src/block.h: the block buffer, its 16350-byte limit and the
      "<n>w\0<lines>" block header.
    - brlaser src/job.cc: begin_job (128 NUL bytes, PJL JOB), end_job
      (PJL EOJ, UEL), write_page_header (PJL RAS1200MODE, RESOLUTION,
      ECONOMODE, SOURCETRAY, MEDIATYPE, PAPER, PAGEPROTECT, ORIENTATION,
      ENTER LANGUAGE = PCL, ESC E, copies ESC&l<n>X, duplex ESC&l2S),
      encode_page (64-line bands, ESC*b1030m ... 1030M FF), the job-name
      character filter, and re-sending the page header only when the page
      parameters change.
    - brlaser src/main.cc: build_page_params (tray names, PPD page size
      name to PJL PAPER mapping, cupsInteger10 economode) and
      ascii_job_name.

  src/raster.rs
    - The 1-bit/1-colour/10000-byte-line checks from brlaser src/main.cc.
      The raster parser itself is new code written from the CUPS raster
      format description.

  src/dcp1600.ppd
    - Derived from the "DCP-1600 series" entry of brlaser brlaser.drv
      (page sizes, 600 dpi K 1-bit resolution, PLAIN media type,
      brlaserEconomode option), trimmed, with the imageable area set to the
      full page so Apple's cgpdftoraster renders whole-page raster.
